00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:50.000
come up, might be just a wise crack in a conversation or something, but that's where a lot of the ideas come from. So, in 1961, you can introduce an octagon and have it be pretty simple, be bold, and be associated with Chase because Chase is so big. Now, the octagon, it's closed off. You can't put an octagon out there as an abstract mark for a company. Is it harder to have a bold graphic that's simple today, just because of the number of shapes or just limited in the world?

