Well, it is hard. Yes, there are so many. And now with little icons and emojis and whatever, there's just so much around. So yes, it is difficult. What we do now is before we show anything to our clients, we have done a preliminary legal search. So we try not to show anything to a client that hasn't at least passed the initial, what they call a knockout search, because we don't want them to fall in

27
00:17:22.000 --> 00:18:06.000
love with something and then find out, you know, if they can't use it. Have you ever fallen in love with something and found out you couldn't use it? Oh, sure. We just don't show it. No, I mean, very much. And one of the one of the complications is of course things are registered as marks with the end of a certain area of business. For example, I'm one example we give is the red star. So obviously, represents China, but it's also Macy's. It's San Pellegrino, it's Heineken. It's many different things, and they're all doing it legally. They will have the right to use it, and we're another. So, it's not

